                <pb facs="0650" n="538" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg538"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1164: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Technical Board</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stevens</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-25T18:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">October 25,
                                1919, 6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 25, 4:40
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your cable October 22, 6 p.m. Have no anxiety, there will [be] no abandonment the
                    work of Service Corps unless the Bolshevik runs some of them out.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stevens</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
